WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.360 --> 00:00:03.890
SPEAKER: Now more
than ever, buyers

00:00:03.890 --> 00:00:06.230
are turning to cloud
marketplaces to fulfill

00:00:06.230 --> 00:00:07.640
their procurement needs.

00:00:07.640 --> 00:00:09.830
As marketplaces are
poised to capture

00:00:09.830 --> 00:00:12.740
a significant percentage
of the $230 billion

00:00:12.740 --> 00:00:16.129
SaaS and Cloud software
market in 2021,

00:00:16.129 --> 00:00:18.770
learn how you can purchase
multiple solution types--

00:00:18.770 --> 00:00:21.980
SaaS, VMs, containers,
datasets, and APIs--

00:00:21.980 --> 00:00:25.340
on Google Cloud Marketplace
that are vetted by Google Cloud

00:00:25.340 --> 00:00:27.900
to cover your
enterprise's IT needs.

00:00:27.900 --> 00:00:30.710
All of this with a single bill
and the ease of deployment

00:00:30.710 --> 00:00:33.180
you've never seen before.

00:00:33.180 --> 00:00:36.390
Google Cloud Marketplace is
a modern procurement platform

00:00:36.390 --> 00:00:39.330
offering a diverse selection
of security, database,

00:00:39.330 --> 00:00:41.490
networking solutions, and more.

00:00:41.490 --> 00:00:44.550
This video will walk you through
how Google Cloud Marketplace

00:00:44.550 --> 00:00:47.400
improves your IT solution
buying experience

00:00:47.400 --> 00:00:49.800
and empowers your
procurement team to procure

00:00:49.800 --> 00:00:53.190
and fulfill fast with a
single bill from Google.

00:00:53.190 --> 00:00:55.140
The Marketplace has
both Google Cloud

00:00:55.140 --> 00:00:57.510
products and partner
solutions to ensure you

00:00:57.510 --> 00:00:59.220
can find exactly what you need.

00:00:59.220 --> 00:01:03.495
[MUSIC PLAYING]

00:01:07.300 --> 00:01:09.870
Let's begin by navigating
to the Marketplace.

00:01:09.870 --> 00:01:11.760
There are three ways to do this.

00:01:11.760 --> 00:01:14.340
If you're not logged in to
the Google Cloud console,

00:01:14.340 --> 00:01:16.860
you can access the
Marketplace homepage by typing

00:01:16.860 --> 00:01:21.990
in cloud.google.com/marketplace,
or just searching for Google

00:01:21.990 --> 00:01:23.423
Cloud Marketplace.

00:01:23.423 --> 00:01:24.840
If you are in your
console, you'll

00:01:24.840 --> 00:01:27.900
see the Marketplace in
the left navigation bar.

00:01:27.900 --> 00:01:30.390
One final way to access
the Marketplace is via

00:01:30.390 --> 00:01:32.640
what's called a [? cameo. ?]
[? Cameos ?] show

00:01:32.640 --> 00:01:35.100
the Marketplace in the context
of your current console

00:01:35.100 --> 00:01:38.610
location, offering a Marketplace
experience that is personalized

00:01:38.610 --> 00:01:39.880
to your needs.

00:01:39.880 --> 00:01:42.960
Once you reach the Marketplace
homepage, browse anonymously,

00:01:42.960 --> 00:01:45.270
or if you're interested
in purchasing or seeing

00:01:45.270 --> 00:01:48.570
what you have deployed, log in
using your Google credentials.

00:01:48.570 --> 00:01:50.070
If you know what
you're looking for,

00:01:50.070 --> 00:01:52.290
the Search bar is in
the center of the page,

00:01:52.290 --> 00:01:54.480
or you can browse
shelves that showcase

00:01:54.480 --> 00:01:56.500
the different
solutions available.

00:01:56.500 --> 00:01:57.960
We keep these shelves fresh.

00:01:57.960 --> 00:02:00.210
For instance, we were
the first marketplace

00:02:00.210 --> 00:02:03.090
to add a COVID-19 dataset.

00:02:03.090 --> 00:02:04.950
The other shelves
here feature commonly

00:02:04.950 --> 00:02:07.950
searched for solution
areas, such as VMs,

00:02:07.950 --> 00:02:12.660
GCP services, SaaS, OS,
DevStacks, et cetera.

00:02:12.660 --> 00:02:14.850
On the left side,
you'll see filters.

00:02:14.850 --> 00:02:17.670
These include different types
of products and categories,

00:02:17.670 --> 00:02:19.650
as well as industries,
which are new.

00:02:19.650 --> 00:02:22.080
And we're constantly adding
more to help you easily

00:02:22.080 --> 00:02:23.970
find the right solutions.

00:02:23.970 --> 00:02:26.790
Google Cloud products can be
found under the Google Cloud

00:02:26.790 --> 00:02:29.337
Platform filter.

00:02:29.337 --> 00:02:34.826
[MUSIC PLAYING]

00:02:38.330 --> 00:02:40.910
Let's say you want to
browse virtual machines.

00:02:40.910 --> 00:02:43.760
Begin by clicking Virtual
Machines to see the VM

00:02:43.760 --> 00:02:46.470
solutions we have before
filtering further.

00:02:46.470 --> 00:02:49.670
Let's say we want to look
for load balancing Ubuntu.

00:02:49.670 --> 00:02:52.880
From here, you can explore
a solution in more detail.

00:02:52.880 --> 00:02:55.820
We're going to go ahead and
click on the second one here.

00:02:55.820 --> 00:03:00.290
NGINX Plus Basic, Ubuntu 18.04.

00:03:00.290 --> 00:03:02.510
The right column provides
the technical specs,

00:03:02.510 --> 00:03:05.750
such as what the solution
runs on and its type.

00:03:05.750 --> 00:03:07.610
Further down the
Overview page, there's

00:03:07.610 --> 00:03:10.730
more information about the
solution and company, a pricing

00:03:10.730 --> 00:03:13.340
table, tutorials and
documentation, training

00:03:13.340 --> 00:03:16.700
and support, and the
terms of service.

00:03:16.700 --> 00:03:18.760
Many VM solutions
have free trials

00:03:18.760 --> 00:03:20.320
which are listed at the top.

00:03:20.320 --> 00:03:23.587
Like this one says,
"30-day Trial Available."

00:03:23.587 --> 00:03:27.403
[MUSIC PLAYING]

00:03:32.650 --> 00:03:36.320
Let's take a look at
a SaaS solution next.

00:03:36.320 --> 00:03:38.630
Search for NetApp
and let autocomplete

00:03:38.630 --> 00:03:41.870
suggest NetApp Cloud
Volume Service.

00:03:41.870 --> 00:03:43.910
Click on the first option here.

00:03:43.910 --> 00:03:47.570
As with the VM solution, this
page outlines technical specs.

00:03:47.570 --> 00:03:49.430
And further down
the Overview page,

00:03:49.430 --> 00:03:52.850
there's more information about
the solution and company,

00:03:52.850 --> 00:03:56.750
a pricing table, tutorials
and documentation, training

00:03:56.750 --> 00:03:58.925
and support, and the
terms of service.

00:04:03.080 --> 00:04:05.540
Let's go ahead and hit Purchase.

00:04:05.540 --> 00:04:07.430
Note that only users
that are billing

00:04:07.430 --> 00:04:10.850
admins and at least a project
viewer will be able to do this.

00:04:10.850 --> 00:04:12.380
Once you have
clicked Purchase, you

00:04:12.380 --> 00:04:16.430
can select a plan, preferred
usage fees and specs, and more.

00:04:16.430 --> 00:04:18.560
On the right side,
there's a pricing slider

00:04:18.560 --> 00:04:21.290
to help you more accurately
calculate the overall cost.

00:04:35.720 --> 00:04:37.790
At the bottom are
the terms of service.

00:04:37.790 --> 00:04:39.830
We're looking at building
custom user license

00:04:39.830 --> 00:04:42.420
agreements directly
within the Marketplace.

00:04:42.420 --> 00:04:45.530
But for now you'll see the
terms of the partner and GCP.

00:04:45.530 --> 00:04:47.330
When you Subscribe,
your order will

00:04:47.330 --> 00:04:49.387
go to the vendor for approval.

00:04:49.387 --> 00:04:54.157
[MUSIC PLAYING]

00:04:58.450 --> 00:05:01.690
Next, we're going to look at
what we call Private Offers.

00:05:01.690 --> 00:05:04.030
We know that many developers
purchase pay as you

00:05:04.030 --> 00:05:05.590
go solutions to try them out.

00:05:05.590 --> 00:05:07.570
And then if the
trial goes well, they

00:05:07.570 --> 00:05:09.490
will want to purchase
the solution.

00:05:09.490 --> 00:05:12.250
With Private Offers, you
can get negotiated prices

00:05:12.250 --> 00:05:14.470
from the partner
via the Marketplace.

00:05:14.470 --> 00:05:16.515
From the Details
page, click Contact

00:05:16.515 --> 00:05:17.890
to get in touch
with the partners

00:05:17.890 --> 00:05:22.020
to start negotiating an offer.

00:05:22.020 --> 00:05:24.540
Once the price is negotiated,
the partner simply

00:05:24.540 --> 00:05:27.300
needs to access their
Marketplace Partner Portal

00:05:27.300 --> 00:05:30.105
and fill in the relevant
details to create your discount.

00:05:49.060 --> 00:05:51.670
When this is saved, a URL
will be generated, which

00:05:51.670 --> 00:05:53.380
the vendor will email to you.

00:05:53.380 --> 00:05:54.820
To do this, the
customer will need

00:05:54.820 --> 00:05:56.740
to have billing admin
rights and at least

00:05:56.740 --> 00:05:58.480
be a viewer on the project.

00:05:58.480 --> 00:06:00.970
One additional benefit
is that these purchases

00:06:00.970 --> 00:06:03.790
count towards your Google
Cloud Commit drawdown.

00:06:03.790 --> 00:06:05.680
We're continuously
gathering feedback

00:06:05.680 --> 00:06:06.730
and improving the flow.

00:06:06.730 --> 00:06:11.550
[MUSIC PLAYING]

00:06:15.900 --> 00:06:18.300
Now if you go back to
the Marketplace homepage,

00:06:18.300 --> 00:06:21.660
click on Your Solutions to view
information about everything

00:06:21.660 --> 00:06:23.040
that you've purchased.

00:06:23.040 --> 00:06:24.660
This page shows
you what you need

00:06:24.660 --> 00:06:28.320
to activate, what's
failed, what's expired,

00:06:28.320 --> 00:06:30.780
what's currently
running, and more.

00:06:30.780 --> 00:06:33.300
We're revamping this page
to include order management

00:06:33.300 --> 00:06:34.800
related tasks here, as well.

00:06:38.160 --> 00:06:40.980
If you click on the hamburger
menu on the top left and hit

00:06:40.980 --> 00:06:45.920
Billing, you'll see all the info
about how you're being billed.

00:06:45.920 --> 00:06:47.920
You can see how much
you're spending every month

00:06:47.920 --> 00:06:50.950
and what you're forecasted
to spend this month.

00:06:50.950 --> 00:06:53.950
If you click View Report,
you can drill down further

00:06:53.950 --> 00:06:56.350
by project, or even
change to group

00:06:56.350 --> 00:07:00.680
by SKU for a deeper
understanding of billing cost.

00:07:00.680 --> 00:07:02.870
We also provide the
option to add solutions

00:07:02.870 --> 00:07:05.720
to a private catalog,
an enterprise governance

00:07:05.720 --> 00:07:09.350
tool that enables admins to
take content from Marketplace.

00:07:09.350 --> 00:07:11.690
The private catalog
provides a tool for admins

00:07:11.690 --> 00:07:13.340
to add pre-approved
solutions that

00:07:13.340 --> 00:07:15.980
have been vetted and
verified and follow

00:07:15.980 --> 00:07:19.040
their internal governance
and compliance policies.

00:07:19.040 --> 00:07:21.110
These solutions can come
from the Marketplace

00:07:21.110 --> 00:07:23.660
or can be internally
created solutions.

00:07:23.660 --> 00:07:26.090
Enterprise customers
then have a single place

00:07:26.090 --> 00:07:27.950
to discover approved
solutions that they

00:07:27.950 --> 00:07:31.310
can deploy knowing the solutions
have been approved and verified

00:07:31.310 --> 00:07:33.230
by their Cloud admin.

00:07:33.230 --> 00:07:36.140
Here you can see an example of
a private catalog, which looks

00:07:36.140 --> 00:07:39.010
and feels like the Marketplace.

00:07:39.010 --> 00:07:40.330
Ready to get going?

00:07:40.330 --> 00:07:42.640
Don't forget to
leverage the $300 credit

00:07:42.640 --> 00:07:46.590
that Google Cloud currently
offers to get started.

00:07:46.590 --> 00:07:49.310
Begin by exploring more
than 2,000 solutions

00:07:49.310 --> 00:07:51.800
available on Google
Cloud Marketplace today.

